# Feature Completeness

## Objective

A feature is complete when it works end-to-end for its agreed scope  -  wired, verified, and operable.

## Requirements

- Integrate with existing config, UI, APIs, or data paths as applicable.
- Handle error and empty states users will hit.
- Do not leave "TODO: wire later" in paths presented as done.
- Document non-obvious usage in `/docs` when helpful.

## Scope Boundary

Complete **within** requested scope. Do not expand into unrequested sub-features (`anti-overengineering.mdc`).

## Golden Rule

Half-integrated features are worse than none  -  they fail quietly in production.